{"1-7":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H5707","lemma":"עֵד","tr":"ed","gloss":"witness","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":70},{"base":"H1847","lemma":"דַּ֫עַת","tr":"da·at","gloss":"knowledge","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":92},{"base":"H2450","lemma":"חָכָם","tr":"cha·kham","gloss":"wise","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":138},{"base":"H8193","lemma":"שָׂפָה","tr":"sa·phah","gloss":"lips","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":176},{"base":"H2415","lemma":"חֹטֵר","tr":"cho·ter","gloss":"branch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0018","lemma":"אֵבוּס","tr":"e·vus","gloss":"crib","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3868","lemma":"לוּז","tr":"luz","gloss":"be devious","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H0504","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"cattle","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H1249","lemma":"בַּר","tr":"bar","gloss":"pure","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H0529","lemma":"אֵמֻן","tr":"e·mun","gloss":"faithful","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":31,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"A wife of noble character, who can find? She is far more precious than rubies.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":31,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"Give her the fruit of her hands, and let her works praise her at the gates.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":24,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":27,"source":"openbible","text":"By wisdom a house is built and by understanding it is established;","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":24,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":27,"source":"openbible","text":"through knowledge its rooms are filled with every precious and beautiful treasure.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Better to live on a corner of the roof than to share a house with a quarrelsome wife.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Better to live in the desert than with a contentious and ill-tempered wife.","from":1},{"book":"RUT","chapter":4,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"“We are witnesses,” said the elders and all the people at the gate. “May the LORD make the woman entering your home like Rachel and Leah, who together built up the house of Israel. May you be prosperous in Ephrathah and famous in Bethlehem.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":9,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"The woman named Folly is loud; she is naive and knows nothing.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-14":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3477","lemma":"יָשָׁר","tr":"ya·shar","gloss":"upright","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":119},{"base":"H1870","lemma":"דֶּ֫רֶךְ","tr":"de·rekh","gloss":"way: conduct","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":706},{"base":"H3820","lemma":"לֵב","tr":"lev","gloss":"heart","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":595},{"base":"H0319","lemma":"אַחֲרִית","tr":"a·cha·rit","gloss":"end","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":61},{"base":"H8057","lemma":"שִׂמְחָה","tr":"sim·chah","gloss":"joy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":94},{"base":"H8424","lemma":"תּוּגָה","tr":"tu·gah","gloss":"grief","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H3510","lemma":"כָּאַב","tr":"ka·av","gloss":"to pain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H6175","lemma":"עָרוּם","tr":"a·rum","gloss":"prudent","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H5472","lemma":"סוּג","tr":"sug","gloss":"to turn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H7814","lemma":"שְׂחֹק","tr":"se·choq","gloss":"laughter","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":16,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":48,"source":"both","text":"There is a way that seems right to a man, but its end is the way of death.","from":12},{"book":"MAT","chapter":7,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"Enter through the narrow gate. For wide is the gate and broad is the way that leads to destruction, and many enter through it.","from":12},{"book":"MAT","chapter":7,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"But small is the gate and narrow the way that leads to life, and only a few find it.","from":12},{"book":"PRO","chapter":12,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":42,"source":"both","text":"The way of a fool is right in his own eyes, but a wise man listens to counsel.","from":12},{"book":"GAL","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":28,"source":"both","text":"If anyone thinks he is something when he is nothing, he deceives himself.","from":12},{"book":"ROM","chapter":6,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"What fruit did you reap at that time from the things of which you are now ashamed? The outcome of those things is death.","from":12},{"book":"LUK","chapter":13,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"“Make every effort to enter through the narrow door. For many, I tell you, will try to enter and will not be able.","from":12},{"book":"PRO","chapter":30,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"There is a generation of those who are pure in their own eyes and yet unwashed of their filth.","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"15-22":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6175","lemma":"עָרוּם","tr":"a·rum","gloss":"prudent","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H6612","lemma":"פֶּ֫תִי","tr":"pe·ti","gloss":"simple","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":19},{"base":"H0200","lemma":"אִוֶּ֫לֶת","tr":"iv·ve·let","gloss":"folly","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"H7451","lemma":"רַע","tr":"ra","gloss":"bad: harmful","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":661},{"base":"H2790","lemma":"חָרַשׁ","tr":"cha·rash","gloss":"to plow","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":74},{"base":"H8130","lemma":"שָׂנֵא","tr":"sa·ne","gloss":"to hate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":146},{"base":"H7453","lemma":"רֵעַ","tr":"re·a","gloss":"neighbor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":188},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":538},{"base":"H7116","lemma":"קָצֵר","tr":"qa·tser","gloss":"short","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H3803","lemma":"כָּתַר","tr":"ka·tar","gloss":"to surround","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The wisdom of the prudent is to discern his way, but the folly of fools deceives them.","from":15},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"A patient man has great understanding, but a quick-tempered man promotes folly.","from":17},{"book":"PRO","chapter":22,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The prudent see danger and take cover, but the simple keep going and suffer the consequences.","from":16},{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lordʼs will is.","from":15},{"book":"PRO","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Be not wise in your own eyes; fear the LORD and turn away from evil.","from":16},{"book":"PRO","chapter":4,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Make a level path for your feet, and all your ways will be sure.","from":15},{"book":"PRO","chapter":27,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The prudent see danger and take cover, but the simple keep going and pay the penalty.","from":15},{"book":"PRO","chapter":29,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"An angry man stirs up dissension, and a hot-tempered man abounds in transgression.","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"23-29":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0200","lemma":"אִוֶּ֫לֶת","tr":"iv·ve·let","gloss":"folly","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":25},{"base":"H3374","lemma":"יִרְאָה","tr":"yir·ah","gloss":"fear","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":45},{"base":"H4195","lemma":"מוֹתָר","tr":"mo·tar","gloss":"advantage","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H1927","lemma":"הֲדָרָה","tr":"ha·da·rah","gloss":"adornment","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H7116","lemma":"קָצֵר","tr":"qa·tser","gloss":"short","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H6089","lemma":"עֶ֫צֶב","tr":"e·tsev","gloss":"toil","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4288","lemma":"מְחִתָּה","tr":"me·chit·tah","gloss":"terror","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H4270","lemma":"מַחְסוֹר","tr":"mach·sor","gloss":"need","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H6315","lemma":"פּוּחַ","tr":"pu·ach","gloss":"to breathe","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H0750","lemma":"אָרֵךְ","tr":"a·rekh","gloss":"slow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"My beloved brothers, understand this: Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to anger,","from":29},{"book":"PRO","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"The one who works his land will have plenty of food, but whoever chases fantasies will have his fill of poverty.","from":23},{"book":"ECC","chapter":7,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"Do not be quickly provoked in your spirit, for anger settles in the lap of a fool.","from":29},{"book":"PRO","chapter":19,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"The fear of the LORD leads to life, that one may rest content, without visitation from harm.","from":26},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"A quick-tempered man acts foolishly, and a devious man is hated.","from":29},{"book":"PRO","chapter":12,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"The hand of the diligent will rule, but laziness ends in forced labor.","from":23},{"book":"JER","chapter":32,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"I will give them one heart and one way, so that they will always fear Me for their own good and for the good of their children after them.","from":26},{"book":"JER","chapter":32,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"I will make an everlasting covenant with them: I will never turn away from doing good to them, and I will put My fear in their hearts, so that they will never turn away from Me.","from":26}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"30-35":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7538","lemma":"רָקָב","tr":"ra·qav","gloss":"rottenness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H3820","lemma":"לֵב","tr":"lev","gloss":"heart","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":595},{"base":"H1760","lemma":"דָּחָה","tr":"da·chah","gloss":"to thrust","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H4832","lemma":"מַרְפֵּא","tr":"mar·pe","gloss":"healing","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H3816","lemma":"לְאֹם","tr":"le·om","gloss":"people","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":31},{"base":"H5678","lemma":"עֶבְרָה","tr":"ev·rah","gloss":"fury","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34},{"base":"H6231","lemma":"עָשַׁק","tr":"a·shaq","gloss":"to oppress","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"H2620","lemma":"חָסָה","tr":"cha·sah","gloss":"to seek refuge","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":37},{"base":"H2778","lemma":"חָרַף","tr":"cha·raph","gloss":"to taunt","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":41},{"base":"H7068","lemma":"קִנְאָה","tr":"qin·ah","gloss":"jealousy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":17,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"A joyful heart is good medicine, but a broken spirit dries up the bones.","from":30},{"book":"PSA","chapter":107,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"and fruitful land into fields of salt, because of the wickedness of its dwellers.","from":34},{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"“Now if you faithfully obey the voice of the LORD your God and are careful to follow all His commandments I am giving you today, the LORD your God will set you high above all the nations of the earth.","from":34},{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":68,"verseEnd":68,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD will return you to Egypt in ships by a route that I said you should never see again. There you will sell yourselves to your enemies as male and female slaves, but no one will buy you.”","from":34},{"book":"PRO","chapter":22,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"The rich and the poor have this in common: The LORD is Maker of them all.","from":31},{"book":"JOB","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"For resentment kills a fool, and envy slays the simple.","from":30},{"book":"PRO","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"This will bring healing to your body and refreshment to your bones.","from":30},{"book":"PRO","chapter":4,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Guard your heart with all diligence, for from it flow springs of life.","from":30}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}